  "scope": "Stage4J8: public D3D9 SetStreamSource(NULL) preserves current live offset/stride,including while recording,ignoring supplied metadata. Shared internal stream setter owns exact storage/metadata publication and release; stateblock Apply uses it directly to restore captured NULL metadata rather than normalizing against current live state. Successful UP clears buffer/offset/stride0; indexed UP also clears IB. Actual native methods:40960 new checks,512 pool/slot profiles,4096 NULL preserves,512 recorded-NULL/Capture/Apply sequences,all16 slots,zero stride,duplicate filtering,ignored high incoming metadata,live rather than recorded metadata,exact internal restoration and complete storage cleanup.12 strict assertion mutants,three old actual public Set/Apply/UP controls,ASAN/UBSAN,all retained graph/callback suites. XP uses fiveVB/oneIB,16 slots,70 stream getters,one recorded NULL,two snapshot Applies and one Capture. Two bound strip draws,primitiveUP,indexedUP,post-Reset Clear with exact6 uploads and38 stream/oneIB commands; six accurate buffer destructions. Five simulated XP pixel replies prove transport; dual real GPU320-pixel replay and empty maps before genuine owner release. NonNULL offsets/unaligned hardware-specific acceptance,failed-UP cleanup,FVF converted-declaration identity/cache,D3D8,arbitrary callbacks/thread/loss/full Reset/format/MSAA/fullscreen/multi-buffer/wrapper conversion,native HAL,games/FPS and overall stages4/5/6 remain open. Host/protocol/shader/bundle and D3D8/DDraw unchanged.",
